The session-start template renders the locked block — heading, prose, a two-column Playbook |
Trigger table — over the same playbook list `/playbook` iterates, so inside a project both the
vault's own playbook and the global one appear. Core playbooks are rows too; the render is filtered
to the fixture rows so the case depends on shipped playbooks only through their existence.

-- fixtures/cwd/.booping --
project_name: probe
vault_path: ./vault
latest_migration: 9999
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/config.yaml --
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/_playbooks/fx-local/playbook.md --
---
name: fx-local
title: Local
summary: Project fixture.
trigger: do the local thing; the local | piped thing
---

Preamble.
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/_playbooks/fx-local/playbook.yaml --
graph:
  only: []
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/_playbooks/fx-local/only/prompt.md --
---
name: only
summary: Only step.
---

Only body.
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-global/playbook.md --
---
name: fx-global
title: Global
summary: Global fixture.
trigger: do the global thing
---

Preamble.
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-global/playbook.yaml --
graph:
  only: []
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-global/only/prompt.md --
---
name: only
summary: Only step.
---

Only body.
-- cmd --
sh -c 'booping render src/templates/hooks/session_start.md.j2 | grep -E "^(## booping|This repo|Experiments|\| (Playbook|---|fx-))"'
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
## booping
This repo is a booping project. Project work a playbook below fits — a decision or ADR, a spec record, a plan, a sprint, a review, a retro — goes through that playbook: offer it to the user by name and, once they agree, run `/booping:playbook {name}`; its render brings the project's rules. Project work nothing narrower fits → offer `project-manager`. Questions, explanations and debugging need no playbook.
Experiments, evals and benchmark matrices run in stages — cheap screen → shortlist → significance — with each stage's size (calls, rough cost) and what it decides named before launch ([booping:rule/0039](${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/specs/rule/0039-experiments-run-in-stages.md)).
| Playbook | Trigger |
| --- | --- |
| fx-global | do the global thing |
| fx-local | do the local thing; the local \| piped thing |
-- stderr --
